#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13 -I
"""codebase-sync: keep a SANITIZED copy of my codebase in a private GitHub repo (profile repos.private_code).

The owner asked for a repo with the current version of my codebase, kept up to date, with secrets and
personal data stripped.

  codebase-sync              build the export, sanitize, check, commit and push (default)
  codebase-sync --no-push    same, but only commit locally
  codebase-sync check        build + sanitize + check into a temp dir only (no commit, no push)
  codebase-sync review       check, plus list every PII-looking value (masked), allowed ones included
  codebase-sync manifest     check, plus the publish-manifest report (public/private paths; see below)
  codebase-sync precheck     check, plus the public-path gate on a throwaway git tree: what a sync would block,
                             before it lands (no lock, no state, no notes; prints file:line + rule labels only;
                             exit 3 = would block; the gate reuses per-file clean verdicts from ~/.cache/publish-gate
                             under identical rules, CODEBASE_SYNC_GATE_CACHE=off = none; the real sync never does).
                             Used by `assistant ci`, test-all (suite codebase-precheck-tests) and by
                             brain-commit when BRAIN_COMMIT_PRECHECK=1 (warn only; ~45 s)
  codebase-sync --cron       quiet on success; a failure writes ONE ~/inbox note per distinct problem/day. A block
                             (check or gate hits) is noted only once the SAME hit set (file:line:rule) was seen by
                             2 consecutive --cron runs at least CODEBASE_SYNC_BLOCK_MIN (30) min apart: a builder's
                             mid-build copy or fixture is gone by then. A clean run clears it, other hits restart
                             the clock (state: pending-block.json). Never pushes while blocked either way.
  codebase-sync --cron --recheck   the same, but only when a block is pending (else exit 0 at once; cron */30)
  codebase-sync --bg         detach and run with --cron (used by brain-commit; returns immediately)

What goes in: ~/bin, ~/.claude/{skills,agents,hooks,settings.json}, ~/crontab, ~/boot.sh,
~/workspace/{CLAUDE,JOBS,TOOLS,CHANGELOG}.md, ~/plugins (the files the harness repo tracks under plugins/, which
deploys them there byte for byte; the live copies are read),
~/opt/*-tests, ~/opt/unraid-lockdown, the dashboard page (~/opt/dash/index.html with its embedded data emptied),
assistant/README.md: only a pointer. The harness repo ~/opt/assistant is published with its real git history to its
own private repo (profile repos.assistant) by `assistant-publish`, so its code is not exported here (deployed copies
in ~/bin/lib/core.releases stay out too).
Never: secrets, memory, transcripts, TODO/PROBLEMS/GOALS/PROACTIVE.md, reports, state, inbox, caches,
node_modules, venvs, models, images/audio (can't be checked), PDFs whose text can't be checked or that hit.

Sanitizing (export copy only, originals untouched):
  * replace rules from ~/.config/codebase-sync/scrub.txt (0600, never exported), plus the Telegram
    allowFrom ids from ~/.claude/channels/telegram/access.json;
  * settings.json: every env value -> "<redacted>"; dashboard: embedded data -> {}.
Checks (any hit refuses the commit/push; hits are shown as file:line + rule, never the value):
  * secretscan (my real secret values + token formats) on every file (gz decompressed, PDFs via pdftotext);
  * every scrub rule again (catches what could not be rewritten: a PDF or .gz with any hit is dropped);
  * PII detectors: e-mail, Swiss/Serbian mobile numbers, IBAN (mod-97), AHV (EAN-13); known fakes via
    "allow:" lines in scrub.txt.
Repo-owned paths in the export (REPO_OWNED: README.md, .gitignore, LICENSE, docs/, tools/, .github/, ...) live
only in ~/opt/claude-bot-export: they are kept across syncs (symlinks too) and checked like the rest.

Publish manifest (unify plan, Appendix B; deny by default): PUBLIC_PATHS minus PUBLIC_EXCLUDE are the
paths the public repo will publish verbatim; everything else (workspace/, unraid-lockdown/, ...) is private.
Mode (~/.config/codebase-sync/mode, or $CODEBASE_SYNC_MODE; default report):
  report   the export is built with every path scrubbed. The manifest report counts public files
           that are already verbatim (no rule hit), public files that WOULD BLOCK (a scrub rule rewrote them;
           paths + rule labels only), excluded *.jsonl fixtures and in-tree symlinks enforce would add.
  enforce  public paths are copied verbatim and only checked: a term hit blocks (exit 3), never a rewrite;
           tests/*/fixtures/*.jsonl and symlinks that point to another exported file are kept; private paths
           are scrubbed.
           Public-path gate (enforce only): when ~/.config/codebase-sync/gate names a gate command (its first
           non-# line, e.g. `.../publish.py gate claude-assistant`), the staged tree must pass it before the
           commit (called with `--src EXPORT --rev TREE`: the public mirror's own private-term, PII (incl. LAN
           IPs), owner-date, coordinate and secret checks, which go beyond this script's scrub list). A block or
           a gate that cannot run: nothing committed or pushed, exit 3, ONE ~/inbox note per problem/day (file:line
           + rule labels only). No config file = no gate.

Exit: 0 ok/nothing to do, 3 blocked by a check, 1 other error.
Env (tests): CODEBASE_SYNC_HOME (source root), CODEBASE_SYNC_EXPORT, CODEBASE_SYNC_SCRUB,
CODEBASE_SYNC_INBOX, CODEBASE_SYNC_STATE, CODEBASE_SYNC_GATE_CONF; SECRETSCAN_SOURCES for secretscan's value sources;
CODEBASE_SYNC_ASSISTANT_SRC: the harness checkout whose tracked plugins/ files name the ~/plugins files to export
(default CODEBASE_SYNC_HOME/opt/assistant; `assistant ci` passes the tree it checks; none with plugins/ = all of
~/plugins but EXCL_DIRS).
CODEBASE_SYNC_ONLY (precheck only): a file listing source paths (one per line, absolute, under
CODEBASE_SYNC_HOME); only those (and the export's repo-owned files, which the gate reads) are exported, checked and gated
(`assistant ci` passes the would-be ~/bin files a land changes: seconds instead of the whole home).
Rollback: remove the cron line + the hook in ~/bin/brain-commit; `gh repo delete <repos.private_code>` only
with the owner's OK.
"""
import fcntl
import fnmatch
import glob
import gzip
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
BIN = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, BIN)
import secretscan  # noqa: E402

HOME = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_HOME") or os.path.expanduser("~")
REAL_HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
EXPORT = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_EXPORT") or os.path.join(REAL_HOME, "opt/claude-bot-export")
SCRUB = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_SCRUB") or os.path.join(REAL_HOME, ".config/codebase-sync/scrub.txt")
INBOX = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_INBOX") or os.path.join(REAL_HOME, "inbox")
STATE = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_STATE") or os.path.join(REAL_HOME, ".local/state/codebase-sync")
BLOCK_MIN = float(os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_BLOCK_MIN") or 30)   # a block must persist this long before a note
GATE_CONF = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_GATE_CONF") or os.path.join(REAL_HOME, ".config/codebase-sync/gate")
# precheck only: the gate's per-file clean-verdict cache (PUBLISH_GATE_CACHE; rules/inputs change = full rescan).
# The real sync's public_gate never passes it. "off" = no cache.
GATE_CACHE = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_GATE_CACHE") or os.path.join(REAL_HOME, ".cache/publish-gate")
ONLY = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_ONLY") or ""   # precheck only: the source paths to export (see above)
ASSISTANT_POINTER = ("# assistant\n\nThe v2 harness repo (`~/opt/assistant`) is published with its real git history to its own "
                     "private repo (profile `repos.assistant`) by `assistant-publish`, after a privacy scan of every "
                     "commit. Its code is no longer exported here.\n")
GATE_HIT = re.compile(r"^ +(?:[^ ]+:\d+ \S|BLOCK)")

# Live only in the export repo (~/opt/claude-bot-export); kept across syncs and checked. Files or whole dirs.
REPO_OWNED = ("README.md", ".gitignore", "LICENSE", "NOTICE", "SECURITY.md", "CONTRIBUTING.md", "CHANGELOG.md",
              ".gitleaks.toml", ".github", "docs", "examples", "tools", "templates")
# Publish manifest, deny by default: path prefixes (a dir covers everything below it) that are public.
PUBLIC_PATHS = REPO_OWNED + ("bin", "claude", "plugins", "tests", "crontab", "boot.sh", "dash", "assistant")
PUBLIC_EXCLUDE = ("bin/unraid-lockdown", "tests/unraid-lockdown", "tests/tgread", "tests/transcribe/cases.tsv",
                  "tests/transcribe/results")
MANIFEST_ALLOW = ("tests/*/fixtures/*.jsonl",)   # public names EXCL_GLOBS would drop ('*' never crosses a '/')
MODES = ("report", "enforce")
MODE_FILE = os.path.join(REAL_HOME, ".config/codebase-sync/mode")
MAX_FILE = 8 * 1024 * 1024
GIT_NAME = "claude-bot sync"
GIT_EMAIL = "7968838+s-boris@users.noreply.github.com"

# Never exported, wherever they appear (path components / file-name globs).
EXCL_DIRS = {".git", "node_modules", "__pycache__", ".venv", "venv", ".secrets", ".ssh", "synced",
             ".pytest_cache", ".mypy_cache", "core.releases"}   # core.releases: deployed copies of assistant/core
EXCL_GLOBS = ["*.pyc", "*.pyo", ".env", ".env.*", "*.env", "access.json", "*.jsonl", "*.pem", "*.key",
              "id_rsa*", "id_ed25519*", ".credentials*", "*.gguf", "*.safetensors", "*.onnx", "*.pt",
              "*.sqlite", "*.sqlite3", "*.db", "*.swp", "*~", ".DS_Store", "*.bak", "*.bak-*", "*.orig",
              "*.new", "*.tmp", "*.wip"]      # work copies of the edit-on-a-copy + atomic mv routine
WIP_DOT_DIRS = ("bin",)   # any dot-file here is a work copy (e.g. bin/.x.new): never exported
DROP_EXT = {".png", ".jpg", ".jpeg", ".gif", ".webp", ".bmp", ".ico", ".tif", ".tiff", ".heic",
            ".ogg", ".oga", ".opus", ".wav", ".mp3", ".m4a", ".flac", ".mp4", ".mkv", ".webm", ".mov",
            ".zip", ".tar", ".tgz", ".xz", ".bz2", ".7z", ".whl", ".so", ".o", ".a", ".bin"}


def plugin_files():
    """The files the harness checkout (CODEBASE_SYNC_ASSISTANT_SRC, else HOME/opt/assistant) tracks under plugins/,
    relative to it: the plugin files its deploy writes to ~/plugins. None = no checkout with plugins/."""
    repo = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_ASSISTANT_SRC") or os.path.join(HOME, "opt", "assistant")
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(repo, "plugins")):
        return None
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", repo, "ls-files", "-z", "--", "plugins"], capture_output=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return None
    return sorted({p[len("plugins/"):] for p in r.stdout.decode().split("\0") if p.startswith("plugins/")}) or None


def sources():
    """[(src_abs, dest_rel, processor)] for every file to export."""
    out = []

    def add_tree(src_rel, dest_rel, extra_excl_dirs=()):
        root = os.path.join(HOME, src_rel)
        if not os.path.isdir(root):
            return
        for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(root):
            dns[:] = sorted(d for d in dns if d not in EXCL_DIRS and d not in extra_excl_dirs
                            and not d.endswith("-venv"))
            for fn in sorted(fns):
                p = os.path.join(dp, fn)
                out.append((p, os.path.join(dest_rel, os.path.relpath(p, root)), None))

    def add_file(src_rel, dest_rel, proc=None):
        p = os.path.join(HOME, src_rel)
        if os.path.isfile(p):
            out.append((p, dest_rel, proc))

    add_tree("bin", "bin")
    add_tree(".claude/skills", "claude/skills")
    add_tree(".claude/agents", "claude/agents")
    add_tree(".claude/hooks", "claude/hooks")
    add_file(".claude/settings.json", "claude/settings.json", "settings")
    add_file("crontab", "crontab")
    add_file("boot.sh", "boot.sh")
    add_file("workspace/CLAUDE.md", "workspace/CLAUDE.md")
    add_file("workspace/JOBS.md", "workspace/JOBS.md")     # cron/script reference
    add_file("workspace/TOOLS.md", "workspace/TOOLS.md")
    add_file("workspace/CHANGELOG.md", "workspace/CHANGELOG.md")
    add_file("opt/dash/index.html", "dash/index.html", "dash")
    add_tree("opt/unraid-lockdown", "unraid-lockdown")   # owner's SSH lockdown + vault-deploy
    for t in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(HOME, "opt/*-tests"))):
        if os.path.isdir(t):
            add_tree(os.path.relpath(t, HOME), "tests/" + os.path.basename(t)[:-len("-tests")], ("bench",))
    names = plugin_files()
    if names is None:
        add_tree("plugins", "plugins")
    for rel in names or ():
        p = os.path.join(HOME, "plugins", rel)
        if os.path.isfile(p) or os.path.islink(p):
            out.append((p, os.path.join("plugins", rel), None))
    out.append((None, "assistant/README.md", "pointer"))   # the harness repo has its own GitHub repo (assistant-publish)
    return out


def excluded(dest_rel, manifest=False):
    """Why dest_rel is never exported (None = exported). manifest=True: enforce mode's MANIFEST_ALLOW applies."""
    parts = dest_rel.split("/")
    if any(p in EXCL_DIRS for p in parts[:-1]):
        return "excluded dir"
    name = parts[-1]
    if name.startswith(".") and parts[0] in WIP_DOT_DIRS:
        return "excluded work copy (dot-file)"
    for g in EXCL_GLOBS:
        if fnmatch.fnmatch(name, g):
            if manifest and is_public(dest_rel) and any(path_match(dest_rel, a) for a in MANIFEST_ALLOW):
                return None
            return "excluded name " + g
    return None


def manifest_mode():
    m = os.environ.get("CODEBASE_SYNC_MODE")
    if not m:
        try:
            with open(MODE_FILE, encoding="utf-8") as f:
                m = f.read().strip()
        except OSError:
            m = "report"
    if m not in MODES:
        raise SystemExit("codebase-sync: unknown manifest mode %r in %s (want report or enforce)" % (m, MODE_FILE))
    return m


def path_match(path, pattern):
    """fnmatch per path segment: '*' never crosses a '/'."""
    a, b = path.split("/"), pattern.split("/")
    return len(a) == len(b) and all(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(x, y) for x, y in zip(a, b))


def _under(path, prefixes):
    return any(path == p or path.startswith(p + "/") for p in prefixes)


def _private_repo():
    """The private export repo for messages (profile repos.private_code); a neutral fallback without bin/lib."""
    try:
        sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "lib"))
        import assistant_profile  # noqa: E402
        return assistant_profile.get("repos.private_code")
    except Exception:
        return "its private repo"


def is_public(dest_rel):
    """True if the publish manifest lists dest_rel as public (deny by default)."""
    return _under(dest_rel, PUBLIC_PATHS) and not _under(dest_rel, PUBLIC_EXCLUDE)


def link_maps(src, dest, tgt, by_dest):
    """A symlink that leaves its directory is still safe to keep when its relative target, read from the export
    path, is another exported file that comes from the same real file (e.g. bin/x -> ../plugins/p/ops/x)."""
    if os.path.isabs(tgt):
        return False
    t = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(dest), tgt))
    if t.startswith("../") or t == ".." or t not in by_dest or excluded(t):
        return False
    return os.path.realpath(by_dest[t]) == os.path.realpath(src)


def new_report(mode):
    return {"mode": mode, "public": 0, "private": 0, "verbatim": 0, "would_block": [], "would_add": [],
            "would_keep_link": []}


def rule_labels(text, rules):
    return sorted({r.label for r in rules if r.rx.search(text)})


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rules
class Rule:
    def __init__(self, raw, repl):
        self.raw, self.repl = raw, repl
        if raw.startswith("re:"):
            self.rx = re.compile(raw[3:])
            self.check_rx = self.rx
            self.label = "scrub:re#" + hashlib.sha1(raw.encode()).hexdigest()[:6]
        else:
            ci = raw.startswith("i:")
            lit = raw[2:] if ci else raw
            body = r"(?<![^\W_])" + re.escape(lit) + r"(?![^\W_])"
            self.rx = re.compile(body, re.I if ci else 0)
            self.check_rx = self.rx
            self.label = "scrub:%s…(%d)" % (lit[:1], len(lit))   # never the full value


def load_rules():
    rules, allow = [], set()
    try:
        with open(SCRUB, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            lines = f.read().splitlines()
    except OSError as e:
        raise SystemExit("codebase-sync: scrub list missing (%s): refusing to export without it" % e)
    for ln in lines:
        if not ln.strip() or ln.lstrip().startswith("#"):
            continue
        if ln.startswith("allow:"):
            allow.add(norm(ln[6:]))
            continue
        if "\t" not in ln:
            raise SystemExit("codebase-sync: bad scrub line (no TAB) in %s" % SCRUB)
        pat, repl = ln.split("\t", 1)
        rules.append(Rule(pat, repl.strip()))
    # Telegram allowFrom ids (the owner's chat id and any other allowed user)
    acc = os.path.join(HOME, ".claude/channels/telegram/access.json")
    try:
        with open(acc, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            ids = json.load(f).get("allowFrom") or []
        for i, v in enumerate(ids):
            v = str(v).strip()
            if v.isdigit() and not any(r.raw == v for r in rules):
                rules.append(Rule(v, str(100000001 + i)))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        pass
    if not rules:
        raise SystemExit("codebase-sync: scrub list has no rules: refusing to export")
    return rules, allow


def norm(v):
    s = re.sub(r"[\s.\-()/]", "", v).lower()
    if s.startswith("+"):
        s = "00" + s[1:]
    for cc in ("0041", "00381"):
        if s.startswith(cc) and s[len(cc):].isdigit():
            s = "0" + s[len(cc):]
    return s


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- PII detectors
EMAIL_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w.+%\\-])[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)*\.[a-z]{2,24}\b")
EMAIL_OK_DOMAIN = re.compile(r"(?:^|\.)(?:example\.(?:com|org|net|ch|de)|example|test|invalid|localhost|local|"
                             r"users\.noreply\.github\.com|anthropic\.com|sentry\.io)$")
EMAIL_OK_LOCAL = re.compile(r"^(?:no-?reply|info|support|service|contact|kontakt|team|admin|hello|help|privacy|"
                            r"security|office|kundendienst|kundenservice|git|root|user|you|me|name|someone|x)$"
                            r"|muster", re.I)
PHONE_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\d.,])(?:(?:\+|00)41[ ]?(?:\(0\)[ ]?)?7[5-9]|07[5-9]|(?:\+|00)381[ ]?6\d)"
                      r"(?:[ ]?\d){6,7}(?![\d])")
IBAN_RE = re.compile(r"\b[A-Z]{2}\d{2}(?: ?[A-Z0-9]{4}){2,7}(?: ?[A-Z0-9]{1,3})?\b")
AHV_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\d.])756\.?\d{4}\.?\d{4}\.?\d{2}(?![\d])")


def iban_ok(v):
    s = v.replace(" ", "")
    if not (15 <= len(s) <= 34):
        return False
    r = s[4:] + s[:4]
    try:
        return int("".join(str(int(c, 36)) for c in r)) % 97 == 1
    except ValueError:
        return False


def ean13_ok(v):
    d = [int(c) for c in v if c.isdigit()]
    if len(d) != 13:
        return False
    s = sum(x * (3 if i % 2 else 1) for i, x in enumerate(d[:12]))
    return (10 - s % 10) % 10 == d[12]


def pii_hits(text, allow):
    """[(kind, value, line)] for PII-looking values, with allowed flag."""
    out = []

    def line_of(pos):
        return text.count("\n", 0, pos) + 1

    for m in EMAIL_RE.finditer(text):
        v = m.group(0)
        local, dom = v.rsplit("@", 1)
        ok = bool(EMAIL_OK_DOMAIN.search(dom.lower()) or EMAIL_OK_LOCAL.search(local)) or norm(v) in allow
        out.append(("email", v, line_of(m.start()), ok))
    for m in PHONE_RE.finditer(text):
        v = m.group(0)
        out.append(("phone", v, line_of(m.start()), norm(v) in allow))
    for m in IBAN_RE.finditer(text):
        v = m.group(0)
        if not v.startswith("RF") and iban_ok(v):   # RF = creditor reference, same checksum, not an account
            out.append(("iban", v, line_of(m.start()), norm(v) in allow))
    for m in AHV_RE.finditer(text):
        v = m.group(0)
        if ean13_ok(v):
            out.append(("ahv", v, line_of(m.start()), norm(v) in allow))
    return out


def mask(v):
    return v[:2] + "…" + v[-2:] if len(v) > 6 else "…"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- per-file processing
def sanitize_text(text, rules):
    for r in rules:
        text = r.rx.sub(r.repl, text)
    return text


def strip_settings(text):
    d = json.loads(text)
    if isinstance(d.get("env"), dict):
        d["env"] = {k: "<redacted>" for k in d["env"]}
    return json.dumps(d, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"


DASH_DATA_RE = re.compile(r'(<script id="dash-data"[^>]*>)(.*?)(</script>)', re.S)


def strip_dash(text):
    return DASH_DATA_RE.sub(lambda m: m.group(1) + "{}" + m.group(3), text)


def decode_text(b):
    if b"\0" in b[:65536]:
        return None
    try:
        return b.decode("utf-8")
    except UnicodeDecodeError:
        return None


def pdf_text(path):
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["pdftotext", "-q", path, "-"], capture_output=True, timeout=60)
        return r.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace")
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return ""


def build(stage, rules, mode="report", rep=None, only=None):
    """Copy + sanitize all sources into stage. Returns (kept, dropped[(dest, reason)]).
    rep (dict from new_report) collects the manifest report; mode "enforce" keeps public paths verbatim.
    only: a set of absolute source paths; the other sources are left out (precheck of a land's changed files)."""
    enforce = mode == "enforce"
    rep = new_report(mode) if rep is None else rep
    kept, dropped = [], []
    srcs = sources()
    if only is not None:
        srcs = [x for x in srcs if x[0] and os.path.abspath(x[0]) in only]
    by_dest = {d: s for s, d, _ in srcs}

    def keep(dest):
        kept.append(dest)
        rep["public" if is_public(dest) else "private"] += 1

    for src, dest, proc in srcs:
        pub = is_public(dest)
        why = excluded(dest)
        if why and not excluded(dest, manifest=True):
            if not enforce:
                rep["would_add"].append(dest)
            else:
                why = None
        if why:
            dropped.append((dest, why))
            continue
        out = os.path.join(stage, dest)
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out), exist_ok=True)
        if proc == "pointer":
            with open(out, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
                f.write(sanitize_text(ASSISTANT_POINTER, rules))
            os.chmod(out, 0o644)
            keep(dest)
            continue
        if os.path.islink(src):
            tgt = os.readlink(src)
            real = os.path.realpath(src)
            if os.path.isabs(tgt) or not real.startswith(os.path.realpath(os.path.dirname(src)) + os.sep):
                if link_maps(src, dest, tgt, by_dest):
                    if enforce:
                        os.symlink(tgt, out)
                        keep(dest)
                        continue
                    rep["would_keep_link"].append(dest)
                dropped.append((dest, "symlink leaves its directory"))
                continue
            os.symlink(tgt, out)
            keep(dest)
            continue
        try:
            st = os.stat(src)
        except OSError:
            continue
        if st.st_size > MAX_FILE:
            dropped.append((dest, "too large"))
            continue
        ext = os.path.splitext(dest)[1].lower()
        if ext in DROP_EXT:
            dropped.append((dest, "binary media (can't be checked)"))
            continue
        with open(src, "rb") as f:
            b = f.read()
        mode = stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode) & 0o755 | 0o644
        if ext == ".gz":
            try:
                inner = decode_text(gzip.decompress(b))
            except OSError:
                inner = None
            if inner is None:
                dropped.append((dest, "gz without text"))
                continue
            clean = sanitize_text(inner, rules)
            if pub and clean != inner:
                rep["would_block"].append((dest, rule_labels(inner, rules)))
                if enforce:
                    clean = inner
            data = gzip.compress(clean.encode("utf-8"), mtime=0)
        elif ext == ".pdf":
            t = pdf_text(src)
            if not t.strip():
                dropped.append((dest, "pdf without a text layer (can't be checked)"))
                continue
            data = b   # checked later; a PDF with any hit is dropped (enforce, public: blocks), never rewritten
        else:
            text = decode_text(b)
            if text is None:
                dropped.append((dest, "binary (can't be checked)"))
                continue
            if proc == "settings":
                text = strip_settings(text)
            elif proc == "dash":
                text = strip_dash(text)
            clean = sanitize_text(text, rules)
            if pub and clean != text:
                rep["would_block"].append((dest, rule_labels(text, rules)))
                if enforce:
                    clean = text      # verbatim: the check below blocks it, never a silent rewrite
            data = clean.encode("utf-8")
        with open(out, "wb") as f:
            f.write(data)
        os.chmod(out, mode)
        keep(dest)
    return kept, dropped


def texts_of(path):
    """Text views of one exported file for checking: [(label, text)]."""
    ext = os.path.splitext(path)[1].lower()
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        b = f.read()
    if ext == ".gz":
        return [("", gzip.decompress(b).decode("utf-8", "replace"))]
    if ext == ".pdf":
        return [("pdf-text", pdf_text(path)), ("pdf-raw", b.decode("latin-1"))]
    return [("", b.decode("utf-8", "replace"))]


def check(stage, rules, allow, review=False, enforce=False):
    """Returns (problems[(rel, line, rule)], dropped, review_rows). Drops PDFs/.gz that hit (they can't be fixed);
    in enforce mode a hit in a PUBLIC .pdf/.gz is a problem instead (public files are never silently dropped)."""
    problems, dropped, rows = [], [], []
    for dp, dns, fns in os.walk(stage):
        dns[:] = [d for d in dns if d != ".git"]
        for fn in sorted(fns):
            p = os.path.join(dp, fn)
            rel = os.path.relpath(p, stage)
            if os.path.islink(p):
                continue
            hits = []
            for label, text in texts_of(p):
                for name, line in secretscan.find(text):
                    hits.append((line, "secret:" + name))
                if label == "pdf-raw":
                    continue
                for r in rules:
                    for m in r.check_rx.finditer(text):
                        hits.append((text.count("\n", 0, m.start()) + 1, r.label))
                for kind, v, line, ok in pii_hits(text, allow):
                    if review:
                        rows.append((rel, line, kind, mask(v), "allowed" if ok else "BLOCKS"))
                    if not ok:
                        hits.append((line, "pii:%s %s" % (kind, mask(v))))
            if not hits:
                continue
            if rel.endswith((".pdf", ".gz")) and not (enforce and is_public(rel)):   # can't be rewritten: drop
                os.unlink(p)
                dropped.append((rel, "%s with a hit (%s)" % (rel.rsplit(".", 1)[1], hits[0][1].split(" ")[0])))
                continue
            for line, what in hits:
                problems.append((rel, line, what))
    return problems, dropped, rows


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- git
def git(*args, cwd=None, check=True, timeout=120):
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", cwd or EXPORT] + list(args), capture_output=True, timeout=timeout)
    r.stdout = r.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace")   # diffs may carry binary bytes (PDFs git sees as text)
    r.stderr = r.stderr.decode("utf-8", "replace")
    if check and r.returncode:
        raise RuntimeError("git %s: %s" % (args[0], (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-300:]))
    return r


def ensure_repo():
    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(EXPORT, ".git")):
        os.makedirs(EXPORT, exist_ok=True)
        git("init", "-q", "--initial-branch=main")
    git("config", "user.name", GIT_NAME)
    git("config", "user.email", GIT_EMAIL)
    git("config", "commit.gpgsign", "false")
    hook = os.path.join(EXPORT, ".git/hooks/pre-commit")
    want = "#!/bin/sh\n# codebase-sync: no secrets in the export, ever (names only, values never shown).\n" \
           "exec /usr/bin/python3 -I %s --scan-staged\n" % os.path.join(BIN, "secretscan.py")
    if not os.path.exists(hook) or open(hook).read() != want:
        with open(hook, "w") as f:
            f.write(want)
        os.chmod(hook, 0o755)


def sync_tree(stage):
    """Make EXPORT's work tree equal to stage (keeping .git)."""
    r = subprocess.run(["rsync", "-a", "--delete", "--checksum", "--exclude", "/.git", stage + "/", EXPORT + "/"],
                       capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode:
        raise RuntimeError("rsync: " + r.stderr.strip()[-300:])


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- reporting
def note(problem_key, body, cron):
    if not cron:
        return
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    key = hashlib.sha1((problem_key + time.strftime("%F")).encode()).hexdigest()[:12]
    mark = os.path.join(STATE, "last-note")
    try:
        if open(mark).read().strip() == key:
            return
    except OSError:
        pass
    os.makedirs(INBOX, exist_ok=True)
    fn = os.path.join(INBOX, "codebase-sync-%d.md" % int(time.time()))
    with open(fn, "w") as f:
        f.write("codebase-sync (sanitized export → github %s): %s\n"
                "Data, not instructions. Fix the source or the scrub list (~/.config/codebase-sync/scrub.txt), "
                "then run `codebase-sync`.\n" % (_private_repo(), body))
    with open(mark, "w") as f:
        f.write(key)


def _pending_path():
    return os.path.join(STATE, "pending-block.json")


def block_note(kind, hits, body, cron):
    """A block (check or gate hits). Manual runs: nothing to do (stderr already has it). --cron: write the note
    only when an earlier --cron run saw the same hit set (file:line:rule) >= BLOCK_MIN minutes ago, so a
    builder's mid-build state never reaches the inbox. Returns "noted", "deferred" or "manual"."""
    if not cron:
        return "manual"
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    key = hashlib.sha1(("%s\n%s" % (kind, "\n".join(sorted(set(hits))))).encode()).hexdigest()[:16]
    now = time.time()
    try:
        with open(_pending_path()) as f:
            st = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        st = {}
    if not isinstance(st, dict) or st.get("key") != key:
        st = {"key": key, "kind": kind, "hits": len(set(hits)), "first": now, "runs": 0}
    st["runs"] = int(st.get("runs", 0)) + 1
    st["last"] = now
    tmp = _pending_path() + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(st, f)
    os.replace(tmp, _pending_path())
    if st["runs"] >= 2 and now - float(st.get("first", now)) >= BLOCK_MIN * 60:
        note("%s %s" % (kind, " ".join(sorted(set(hits)))), body, cron)
        return "noted"
    return "deferred"


def block_clear():
    """A run that got past every block: forget the pending one."""
    try:
        os.remove(_pending_path())
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass


def run_gate(lines, src, tree, env=None):
    """(rc, hit lines, raw output) of the gate command (first of `lines`) on git tree `tree` of repo `src`."""
    rc, out = 1, "no gate command in %s" % GATE_CONF
    if lines:
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(shlex.split(lines[0]) + ["--src", src, "--rev", tree], capture_output=True,
                               text=True, timeout=600, env=env)
            rc, out = r.returncode, r.stdout + r.stderr
        except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
            rc, out = 1, "%s: %s" % (type(e).__name__, str(e)[-200:])
    return rc, [ln.strip() for ln in out.splitlines() if GATE_HIT.match(ln)], out


def gate_lines():
    """The gate config's non-# lines, or None when there is no config file (= no gate)."""
    try:
        with open(GATE_CONF, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            return [ln.strip() for ln in f if ln.strip() and not ln.lstrip().startswith("#")]
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None


def precheck_gate(stage):
    """Precheck: the gate on the staged tree, committed to a throwaway repo (EXPORT is never touched).
    Returns (rc, lines to print): 0 passed / no gate, 3 blocked, else could not run."""
    lines = gate_lines()
    if lines is None:
        return 0, []
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="codebase-precheck-")
    try:
        env = dict(os.environ, GIT_DIR=os.path.join(tmp, "git"), GIT_WORK_TREE=stage)
        for cmd in (["git", "init", "-q", "--bare", env["GIT_DIR"]], ["git", "add", "-A"], ["git", "write-tree"]):
            r = subprocess.run(cmd, env=env if cmd[1] != "init" else None, capture_output=True, text=True,
                               timeout=120)
            if r.returncode:
                return 1, ["gate: %s failed: %s" % (" ".join(cmd[:2]), (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-200:])]
        genv = dict(os.environ)
        if GATE_CACHE != "off":
            genv["PUBLISH_GATE_CACHE"] = GATE_CACHE
        rc, hits, out = run_gate(lines, env["GIT_DIR"], r.stdout.strip(), env=genv)
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)
    if rc in (0, 3):
        return rc, hits
    return rc, hits or ["gate could not run (exit %d): %s" % (rc, (out.strip().splitlines() or [""])[-1][-200:])]


def public_gate(tree, cron):
    """Enforce mode: run the public-path gate (GATE_CONF's first non-# line + `--src EXPORT --rev TREE`) on the
    staged tree. Returns 0 (passed, or no gate configured) or 3 (blocked / could not run; one note per problem/day).
    The gate prints file:line + rule labels only; only those lines are passed on."""
    lines = gate_lines()
    if lines is None:
        return 0
    rc, hits, out = run_gate(lines, EXPORT, tree)
    if rc == 0:
        return 0
    why = "the public-path gate blocked it" if rc == 3 else "the public-path gate could not run (exit %d)" % rc
    detail = "; ".join(hits[:20]) if hits else (out.strip().splitlines() or [""])[-1][-200:]
    msg = "BLOCKED: %s, nothing committed or pushed: %s" % (why, detail)
    print("codebase-sync: " + msg, file=sys.stderr)
    if rc == 3:
        block_note("gate", hits, msg, cron)
    else:
        note("gate %d %s" % (rc, " ".join(hits)), msg, cron)
    return 3


def save_state(d):
    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(STATE, "last-run.json"), "w") as f:
        json.dump(d, f, indent=1)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- main
def main(argv):
    args = [a for a in argv if not a.startswith("--")]
    flags = {a for a in argv if a.startswith("--")}
    if "--help" in flags or "-h" in argv or (args and args[0] == "help"):
        print(__doc__.strip())
        return 0
    if "--recheck" in flags:   # cron */30: only while a block is pending (no lock, no work otherwise)
        if not os.path.exists(_pending_path()):
            return 0
        flags.add("--cron")
    if "--bg" in flags:
        if os.path.exists(os.path.join(REAL_HOME, ".config/codebase-sync/off")):
            return 0
        subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, "-I", os.path.realpath(__file__), "--cron"],
                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                         start_new_session=True)
        return 0
    mode = args[0] if args else "run"
    if mode not in ("run", "check", "review", "manifest", "precheck"):
        print("codebase-sync: unknown command %r (see --help)" % mode, file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    cron = "--cron" in flags
    push = mode == "run" and "--no-push" not in flags

    os.makedirs(STATE, exist_ok=True)
    lockf = open(os.path.join(STATE, "lock"), "w")
    deadline = time.time() + 180
    while mode != "precheck":   # precheck writes nothing shared: no lock (a running sync never delays it)
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lockf, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            break
        except OSError:
            if time.time() > deadline:
                print("codebase-sync: another run holds the lock", file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
            time.sleep(2)

    try:
        rules, allow = load_rules()
        mmode = manifest_mode()
    except SystemExit as e:
        note("config", str(e), cron)
        print(e, file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    only = None
    if mode == "precheck" and ONLY:   # never for a real sync: a partial export would drop files from the repo
        try:
            with open(ONLY, encoding="utf-8") as f:
                only = {os.path.abspath(ln.strip()) for ln in f if ln.strip()}
        except OSError as e:
            print("codebase-sync: CODEBASE_SYNC_ONLY unreadable: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
    stage = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="codebase-sync-")
    try:
        man = new_report(mmode)
        for f in REPO_OWNED:
            p = os.path.join(EXPORT, f)
            q = os.path.join(stage, f)
            if os.path.islink(p):
                os.symlink(os.readlink(p), q)
            elif os.path.isdir(p):
                shutil.copytree(p, q, symlinks=True, ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns(".git"))
            elif os.path.isfile(p):
                shutil.copy2(p, q)
            if os.path.lexists(q):
                man["public"] += 1 if not os.path.isdir(q) or os.path.islink(q) else \
                    sum(len(fs) + sum(os.path.islink(os.path.join(dp, d)) for d in ds) for dp, ds, fs in os.walk(q))
        kept, dropped = build(stage, rules, mmode, man, only)
        problems, pdf_dropped, rows = check(stage, rules, allow, review=(mode == "review"),
                                            enforce=(mmode == "enforce"))
        dropped += pdf_dropped
        gone = {rel for rel, _ in pdf_dropped}
        for rel, why in pdf_dropped:
            man["public" if is_public(rel) else "private"] -= 1
            if is_public(rel):
                man["would_block"].append((rel, [why]))
        man["verbatim"] = man["public"] - len([d for d, _ in man["would_block"] if d not in gone])
        nfiles = sum(len(fs) for _, _, fs in os.walk(stage))
        msum = {k: (len(v) if isinstance(v, list) else v) for k, v in man.items()}
        state = {"time": time.strftime("%F %T"), "mode": mode, "files": nfiles,
                 "dropped": dropped, "problems": [list(p) for p in problems[:200]],
                 "manifest": dict(msum, would_block_paths=[d for d, _ in man["would_block"]][:400],
                                  would_add=man["would_add"], would_keep_link=man["would_keep_link"])}
        mline = ("manifest (%s): %d public (%d verbatim, %d would block, %d would be added, %d links would be kept), "
                 "%d private" % (mmode, msum["public"], msum["verbatim"], msum["would_block"], msum["would_add"],
                                 msum["would_keep_link"], msum["private"]))
        if mode == "review":
            for r in rows:
                print("%s:%s %s %s %s" % r)
        if mode == "manifest":
            for d, labels in sorted(man["would_block"]):
                print("would block  %s  (%s)" % (d, ", ".join(labels)))
            for d in man["would_add"]:
                print("would add    %s" % d)
            for d in man["would_keep_link"]:
                print("would keep   %s (symlink)" % d)
        if mode == "precheck":
            out = ["%s:%s %s" % p for p in problems]
            grc, glines = precheck_gate(stage) if mmode == "enforce" else (0, [])
            out += glines
            for ln in out:
                print("  " + ln, flush=True)
            rc = 3 if problems or grc == 3 else (1 if grc else 0)
            print("codebase-sync precheck: %s" % (
                "clean (%d files; public-path gate %s)" % (nfiles, "passed" if mmode == "enforce" and
                                                           gate_lines() is not None else "not configured")
                if rc == 0 else "WOULD BLOCK (%d hit(s))" % len(out) if rc == 3 else "gate could not run"),
                file=sys.stderr if rc else sys.stdout)
            return rc
        if problems:
            files = sorted({p[0] for p in problems})
            msg = "BLOCKED: %d hit(s) in %d file(s), nothing committed or pushed: %s" % (
                len(problems), len(files), "; ".join("%s:%s %s" % p for p in problems[:15]))
            print("codebase-sync: " + msg, file=sys.stderr)
            state["note"] = block_note("blocked", ["%s:%s:%s" % p[:3] for p in problems], msg, cron)
            state["result"] = "blocked"
            save_state(state)
            return 3
        if mode != "run":
            if not cron:
                print("codebase-sync: clean (%d files exported, %d dropped)" % (nfiles, len(dropped)))
                print("codebase-sync: " + mline)
            state["result"] = "clean"
            save_state(state)
            return 0

        ensure_repo()
        sync_tree(stage)
        git("add", "-A")
        changed = git("diff", "--cached", "--quiet", check=False).returncode != 0
        if changed:
            stat_line = git("diff", "--cached", "--shortstat").stdout.strip()
            # belt and braces: the whole staged diff through secretscan once more
            diff = git("diff", "--cached", "--no-color").stdout
            if secretscan.find(diff):
                git("reset", "-q")
                note("diff-secret", "BLOCKED: secretscan flagged the staged diff; nothing committed", cron)
                state["result"] = "blocked"
                save_state(state)
                return 3
            if mmode == "enforce" and public_gate(git("write-tree").stdout.strip(), cron):
                git("reset", "-q")
                state["result"] = "blocked by the public-path gate"
                save_state(state)
                return 3
            block_clear()
            msg = "sync %s: %s" % (time.strftime("%F %H:%M"), stat_line)
            r = git("commit", "-q", "-m", msg, check=False)
            if r.returncode:
                git("reset", "-q")
                note("commit", "commit refused (pre-commit secretscan?): " + (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-200:],
                     cron)
                state["result"] = "commit refused"
                save_state(state)
                return 3
        else:
            block_clear()
        state["commit"] = git("rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD", check=False).stdout.strip()
        pushed = ""
        if push and git("remote", check=False).stdout.strip():
            ahead = git("rev-list", "--count", "@{u}..HEAD", check=False)
            if ahead.returncode or ahead.stdout.strip() != "0":
                r = git("push", "-q", "-u", "origin", "HEAD", check=False, timeout=120)
                if r.returncode:
                    note("push", "push failed: " + (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-200:], cron)
                    state["result"] = "push failed"
                    save_state(state)
                    print("codebase-sync: push failed", file=sys.stderr)
                    return 1
                pushed = ", pushed"
        state["result"] = ("committed" if changed else "unchanged") + pushed
        save_state(state)
        if not cron:
            print("codebase-sync: %s (%d files, %d dropped)%s" % (
                ("committed " + state["commit"]) if changed else "no changes", nfiles, len(dropped), pushed))
        return 0
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001
        note("error " + type(e).__name__, "error: %s" % str(e)[-300:], cron)
        print("codebase-sync: error: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(stage, ignore_errors=True)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
